  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_046 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) is the best result at 0.706 acc. The only prior evidence on aggregation (avgpool vs. transformer) comes from pca_n2000, where avgpool outperformed transformer (0.629 vs 0.599, configs 003 vs 017). However, scvi_n200 produces a fundamentally different learned, nonlinear, low-dimensional representation, so the aggregation ranking may not transfer. Question: config_006 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while keeping scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, and weighted fusion fixed, directly testing whether transformer aggregation can better model interactions in the scvi latent space. Why this is the best next experiment: it is a single-variable, clean comparison against the current best (config_046), it resolves the most important unresolved design question (aggregation) in the context of the dominant RNA encoder, and it could either confirm that avgpool is robustly superior or uncover a further performance gain—both outcomes are highly informative under a limited budget."
}

